Subject: ps2xRecomp: emit tail calls through the function table

A J to a known function start was emitted as a direct C++ call, so PS2Runtime::replaceFunction()
(game overrides) never saw tail calls: FUN_0024cfd8 tail-jumps to rxThInit 0x24bdc8 and the
original ran despite the override. JAL already dispatches through the table; J now does too.

diff --git a/ps2xRecomp/src/lib/control_flow_emitter.cpp b/ps2xRecomp/src/lib/control_flow_emitter.cpp
index 4bf8dc5..b5c7279 100644
--- a/ps2xRecomp/src/lib/control_flow_emitter.cpp
+++ b/ps2xRecomp/src/lib/control_flow_emitter.cpp
@@ -220,7 +220,9 @@ namespace ps2recomp
             return false;
         }
 
-        m_ss << indent << functionName << "(rdram, ctx, runtime); return;\n";
+        // Through the function table, like JAL, so runtime->replaceFunction() overrides also catch tail calls.
+        m_ss << fmt::format("{}runtime->lookupFunction(0x{:X}u)(rdram, ctx, runtime); return; // {}\n",
+                            indent, target, functionName);
         return true;
     }
 
